message:
Adjust parameters of evaluate_{lagrangian/dual}

Since both functions need both arc and node info, might as well
demand the full structure that's meant to keep these things aligned.

Fill out within=, caliper= logic for match_on.{ISM/matrix}

In the process documenting intended semantics of NA, NaN in
match distance objects. Closes #181.

MQ/example9 and 9a. Added possibility to write root files with vectors of data.

Example9:
- run_digiToBin.C - in the macro one may uncomment lines to store data in root files with vectors of data;
- PixelLinkDef.h - added PixelPayload classes to root dictionaries;
Example9a:
- README.md - removed wrongly committed lines;
- startFairMQEx9aFromBin - added option to read from binary or from root file with vectors;
- PixelAltDigiWriteToRootVector - class to write digis to root files with vectors;
- FairMQEx9aSamplerBin - reads from binary or root file with vectors, depending on the name of the file.

MQ/examples/simulation_split

First version of the MC simulation in MQ, where
generated events are sent to transport devices:

- FairMQPrimaryGeneratorDevice - generates events and pushes them;
- FairMQTransportDevices - pulls generated events and transports them in G3 or G4;
- FairGenericStack/FairStack - added new function SetParticleArray();
- FairMQRunDevice - base class for FairMQSimDevice.

examples/MQ/simulation_split

Restructed the simulation_split example.

- FairMQPrimaryGeneratorDevice - now can split simulated events into chunks;
- FairMQTransportDevice - transports full or chunk of simulated events;
- FairMQChunkMerger - merges chunks of individual events into full events;

Added possibility to add more input files to the source in the
FairMQEx9Sampler.

- FairMQEx9Sampler - replaced string with vector of strings to store input file names,
                     changed the SetInputFileName into AddInputFileName;
- runEx9Sampler.cxx - made vector of input file names, calling appropriate function;
- startFairMQEx9New.sh.in - put an example of how to add another input file;
- Pixel - added flag (fMisalignDetector) to steer the execution of the ModifyGeometry() function;
          put back calling of the FairDetector::Initialize() in the Pixel::Initialize();
- PixelGeo - changed getModNumInMod() function to match the Pixel node name;

Allow disabling transfer rate logging per input/output (optional, default is on).

This commit introduces new property to FairMQDevice to control whether rateLogger thread should print rates for a given input/output.
Per default logging is enabled, so existing code works as before and does not need to be updated.
To turn off logging for an initialized input/output, set the `LogInputRate`/`LogOutputRate` property to `0`.

Example:
``` c++
splitter.ChangeState(FairMQSplitter::INIT);
// turn off rate logging for input 1 and output 4
splitter.SetProperty(FairMQSplitter::LogInputRate, 0, 1);
splitter.SetProperty(FairMQSplitter::LogOutputRate, 0, 4);
```

Removed dubious GetObject function from FairSource.
It was replaced by pointers to fChain and fListFolder in the FairRootManager.

- FairSource: removed GetObject function;
- FairFileSource: setting pointers to fInChain and fListFolder in FairRootManager, removed GetObject function;
- FairMixedSource: setting pointers to fBackgroundChain or fSignalChain and fListFolder in FairRootManager, removed GetObject function;
- FairAnaSelector: is storing now pointer to FairFileSource, assuming that no other can be used in PROOF;
- FairRootManager: added pointers to fListFolder and fSourceChain, implemented SetListOfFolders, SetInChain functions, removed GetBGChain, SetInTree;
- FairRunAna: changed determining of the number of events in RunEventReco; virtualized the SetSource function;
- FairRunAnaProof: SetSource function tries to check if the fSource is of FairFileSource;

Conflicts:
	base/source/FairFileSource.cxx

clang-format: Put braces on own line in special cases

Multi-line control statements with the opening brace on the
last line can be a little confusing to read:

```cpp
if (auto foo = something;
    foo.extra_data.check_for(17)) {
    foo.extra_data.check_and_act(19);
}
```

It is not easy to see the end of the condition and the
start of the "then" block.

This gets much easier when putting the opening brace on its
own line:

```cpp
if (auto foo = something;
    foo.extra_data.check_for(17))
{
    foo.extra_data.check_and_act(19);
}
```

