- scripts - added --channel-name data to the parameter MQ server.

MQ/example9 - Slight modifications:
- removed obsolete PixelFindHits::ExecMQ(Option_t*);
- introduced new option to macro run_digiToBin() to enable data storing on different level;
- changed PixelPayload to have common types;

Created FairSink to store output data.

- FairSink - abstract class;
- FairFileSink - implementation to store data in file;
- FairRootManager - calls to file exchanged by FairSink;
- FairRun- changed calls to FairRootManager;
- FairMCApplication - changed calls to FairRootManager;
- FairRunSim - changed calls to FairRootManager;
- FairRunAna - changed calls to FairRootManager;
- FairRunAnaProof - changed calls to FairRootManager;
- FairRunOnline - changed calls to FairRootManager;

MQ/Example9. Added possibility to read and write digis from and to binary files:

- PixelDigiWriteToBinFile - writes PixelDigis to binary file(s);
- PixelDigiBinSource - read PixelDigis from binary file;
- run_dBinSource.C and run_digiToBin.C - to run the classes;
- plus some minor changes to shell scripts

MQ/examples 9 and 9a. Introduced possibility to aggregate a certain number of events
info one MQ message. With this option one may control the average size of message.
This gives possibility to optimize the transfer.

FairMQEx9aSamplerBin - introduced posibility to aggregate more events into one message,
SetAggregateFactor() to set the number of events per message;
FairMQEx9FileSinkBin - is able to read messages with varying number of events;
FairMQEx9aTaskProcessorBin - is able to read messages with varying number of events;
runEx9aSamplerBin.cxx - use the aggregate fuction;
startFairMQEx9aFromBin.sh.in - use the aggregate fuction;
startFairMQEx9aFromBin_Static.sh.in - use the aggregate fuction.

FairSink modifications:

- renamed FairFileSink to FairRootFileSink;
- FairRootFileSink - added functions to get and set ouptut file name;
- replaced SetOutputFile by SetSink in multiple macros;
- FairRadGridManager stores histograms in separate output file;
- FairMCApplication - fixed setting output file name when running multi-threaded;
- FairMonitor - fixed printing summary and storing output to a file;
- ParameterMQServer - added protection against empty fFirstInputName;
